    "synopsis": {
        "native": "\u00c9t\u00e9 1918. La guerre fait rage pour quelques mois encore, mais pour Charles et Ang\u00e8le, elle est d\u00e9j\u00e0 finie. Lui, officier de cavalerie y a laiss\u00e9 une jambe. Elle, son infirmi\u00e8re \u00e0 domicile, vient de perdre au front son grand amour, le p\u00e8re de sa petite fille. Unis par le besoin de se reconstruire, ils nouent une complicit\u00e9 joyeuse qui les ram\u00e8ne \u00e0 la vie. Sur l'insistance de Charles, Ang\u00e8le accepte un mariage de raison. Il leur faudra entrer en guerre, contre eux-m\u00eames et contre l'autre avant d'accepter l'\u00e9vidence de la passion qui les lie malgr\u00e9 eux\u2026",
        "english": "Summer 1918. War still rages for a few months more, but for Charles and Ang\u00e8le, it is already over. He's a cavalry officer who lost one of his legs in battle. She is his home care nurse whose true love, the father of her young daughter, recently died at the Front. United by the need to rebuild their lives, a joyful complicity grows between them which reawakens them to life. At Charles's insistence, Ang\u00e8le accepts a marriage of convenience. They must engage in warfare, against themselves and each other before accepting the obviousness of the passion that unites them despite themselves..."
    },
